"fügt `<meta-data android:name=\"com.google.android.wearable.standalone\" "
"android:value=\"true\" />` hinzu"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:88
msgid "adds `implementation(\"androidx.wear:wear:1.3.0\")`"
msgstr "fügt `implementation(\"androidx.wear:wear:1.3.0\")` hinzu"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:89
msgid "raises `minSdk` to 30 (Wear OS 3, the Google Play floor for watch APKs)"
msgstr "erhöht `minSdk` auf 30 (Wear OS 3, der Google Play Boden für Uhr APKs)"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:90
msgid ""
"Runs `./gradlew assembleDebug`, debug-signs, then `adb install` + launches "
"and streams `logcat`."
msgstr ""
"Läuft `./gradlew assembleDebug`, Debug-Zeichen, dann `adb install` + startet "
"und streamt `logcat`."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:93
msgid "`wear` and `wear-os` are accepted as aliases for `wearos`."
msgstr "`wear` und `wear-os` werden als Aliase für `wearos` akzeptiert."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:97
msgid ""
"Identical to [Android](android.md) — the same `perry/ui` widgets map to the "
"same Android `View` classes (`Text` → `TextView`, `VStack` → vertical "
"`LinearLayout`, `Button` → `Button`, `ScrollView` → `ScrollView`, and so "
"on). No Wear-specific widget API is required: an Android UI tree renders "
"directly on a watch."
msgstr ""
"Identisch zu [Android](android.md) — die gleichen `perry/ui` Widgets Karte "
"zu den gleichen Android `View` Klassen (`Text` → `TextView`, `VStack` → "
"vertikal `LinearLayout`, `Button` → `Button`, `ScrollView` → `ScrollView`, "
"und so weiter). Es wird keine Wear-spezifische Widget-API benötigt: ein "
"Android UI-Baum rendert direkt auf einer Uhr."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:102
msgid ""
"The `androidx.wear` dependency in the overlay brings in `BoxInsetLayout` and "
"swipe-to-dismiss so round screens and the back gesture behave like a native "
"Wear app."
msgstr ""
"Die `androidx.wear`-Abhängigkeit im Overlay bringt `BoxInsetLayout` und "
"Swipe-to-Dismiss so runde Bildschirme und die Rückengeste verhalten sich wie "
"eine native Wear-App."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:108
msgid ""
"A Wear OS app uses the same `App({...})` entry point as every other Perry UI "
"target:"
msgstr ""
"Eine Wear OS-App verwendet den gleichen `App({...})`-Eingangspunkt wie jedes "
"andere Perry-UI-Ziel:"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:111
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"import { App, Text, VStack, Button, State } from \"perry/ui\"\n"
"\n"
"const count = State(0)\n"
"\n"
"App({\n"
"    title: \"My Watch App\",\n"
"    width: 200,\n"
"    height: 200,\n"
"    body: VStack(8, [\n"
"        Text(\"Hello, Wear OS!\"),\n"
"        Text(`Taps: ${count.value}`),\n"
"        Button(\"Tap me\", () => count.set(count.value + 1)),\n"
"    ]),\n"
"})\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"import { App, Text, VStack, Button, State } from \"perry/ui\"\n"
"\n"
"const count = State(0)\n"
"\n"
"App({\n"
"    title: \"My Watch App\",\n"
"    width: 200,\n"
"    height: 200,\n"
"    body: VStack(8, [\n"
"        Text(\"Hello, Wear OS!\"),\n"
"        Text(`Taps: ${count.value}`),\n"
"        Button(\"Tap me\", () => count.set(count.value + 1)),\n"
"    ]),\n"
"})\n"
"```"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:128
msgid ""
"Under the hood this is the Android lifecycle: `PerryActivity` loads "
"`libperry_app.so`, calls into your compiled `main()` over JNI, and the "
"`perry/ui` tree is realized as Android `View`s on the watch."
msgstr ""
"Unter der Haube befindet sich der Android Lebenszyklus: `PerryActivity` lädt "
"`libperry_app.so`, ruft in Ihre kompilierte `main()` über JNI, und der "
"`perry/ui` Baum wird als Android `View` auf der Uhr realisiert."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:134
msgid "Reactive state works exactly as on Android and the other platforms:"
msgstr ""
"Reaktiver Zustand funktioniert genau wie auf Android und den anderen "
"Plattformen:"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:154
msgid ""
"Because the runtime target triple is `aarch64-linux-android`, a Wear OS app "
"reports the **Android** platform number — `__platform__ === 2`:"
msgstr ""
"Da das Laufzeitziel-Dreifach `aarch64-linux-android` ist, meldet eine Wear "
"OS App die **Android** Nummer der Plattform — `__platform__ === 2`:"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:180
msgid ""
"There is intentionally no separate Wear OS platform constant: at runtime a "
"Wear app _is_ an Android app. Branch on screen size at runtime if you need "
"watch-specific layout."
msgstr ""
"Es gibt absichtlich keine separate Wear OS Plattformkonstante: zur Laufzeit "
"eine Wear App _is_ eine Android App. Zweig auf Bildschirmgröße zur Laufzeit, "
"wenn Sie watch-spezifische Layout benötigen."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:186
msgid ""
"Wear OS reuses the `[android]` section of `perry.toml` (bundle id, etc.):"
msgstr ""
"Wear OS verwendet den `[android]`-Abschnitt von `perry.toml` (Bundle id, "
"etc.):"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:188
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"[android]\n"
"bundle_id = \"com.example.mywatch\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```toml\n"
"[android]\n"
"bundle_id = \"com.example.mywatch\"\n"
"```"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:195
msgid ""
"Wear OS inherits Android's widget set but the watch form factor imposes the "
"usual constraints:"
msgstr ""
"Wear OS erbt das Android-Widget-Set, aber der Uhrenformfaktor setzt die "
"üblichen Einschränkungen auf:"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:198
msgid ""
"**Small round screens** — design for ~1.2–1.4\" displays; prefer "
"`ScrollView` and short labels. Use the `androidx.wear` `BoxInsetLayout` "
"insets for round bezels."
msgstr ""
"**Kleine runde Bildschirme** — Design für ~1.2–1.4\"-Displays; lieber "
"`ScrollView` und kurze Etiketten. Verwenden Sie die `androidx.wear` "
"`BoxInsetLayout`-Einsätze für runde Lünetten."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:201
msgid "**Touch-only** — no hover or right-click."
msgstr "**Berührungslos** — kein Schweben oder Rechtsklick."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:202
msgid "**Single window** — modal flows map to `Dialog` views, same as Android."
msgstr ""
"**Einzelfenster** — Modal fließt Karte zu `Dialog` Ansichten, wie Android."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:203
msgid ""
"**Battery / memory** — keep apps lightweight; Wear devices have far less RAM "
"than phones."
msgstr ""
"**Batterie/Speicher** — Apps leicht halten; Verschleißgeräte haben weit "
"weniger RAM als Telefone."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:205
msgid ""
"**Publishing** — Wear apps ship through Google Play as Android APK/AABs (the "
"`perry publish` flow treats Wear like Android)."
msgstr ""
"**Verlagswesen** — Wear apps ship through Google Play als Android APK/AABs "
"(der `perry publish` Fluss behandelt Wear wie Android)."

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:210
msgid "[Android](android.md) — the shared backend, UI mapping, and APK details"
msgstr ""
"[Android](android.md) — das freigegebene Backend, UI-Mapping und APK-Details"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:211
msgid "[Wear OS Tiles](../widgets/wearos.md) — glanceable Tile surfaces"
msgstr "[Wear OS Fliesen](../widgets/wearos.md) — Sichtbare Fliesenoberflächen"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:212 src/platforms/web.md:24
msgid "[Platform Overview](overview.md) — all platforms"
msgstr "[Plattform-Überblick](overview.md) — alle Plattformen"

#: src/platforms/wearos.md:213
msgid "[UI Overview](../ui/overview.md) — the `perry/ui` system"
msgstr "[UI Überblick](../ui/overview.md) — das `perry/ui`-System"

#: src/platforms/harmonyos.md:3
msgid ""
"Perry compiles TypeScript apps for HarmonyOS NEXT (Huawei's mobile OS) by "
"emitting **declarative ArkUI** alongside a logic-only `.so` library. The "
"same TypeScript source that targets macOS, iOS, Android, Linux, and Windows "
"also runs natively on HarmonyOS — no platform-specific adapters needed in "
"user code."
msgstr ""
"Perry kompiliert TypeScript-Apps für HarmonyOS NEXT (Huaweis Mobil-OS), "
"indem es **deklaratives ArkUI** zusammen mit einer reinen Logik-`.so`-"
"Bibliothek emittiert. Derselbe TypeScript-Quellcode, der auf macOS, iOS, "
"Android, Linux und Windows zielt, läuft auch nativ auf HarmonyOS — keine "
"plattformspezifischen Adapter im User-Code nötig."

#: src/platforms/harmonyos.md:7
msgid ""
"HarmonyOS NEXT runs apps via the ArkTS runtime, which owns the UI tree. "
"Perry can't lower `perry/ui` calls to the imperative AppKit/UIKit/etc shape "
"used on every other platform — it has to play by ArkTS's declarative rules. "
"So the harmonyos target is structured differently:"
msgstr ""
"HarmonyOS NEXT führt Apps über die ArkTS-Laufzeit aus, der den UI-Baum "
"gehört. Perry kann `perry/ui`-Aufrufe nicht in die imperative AppKit-/UIKit-/"
"etc-Form herunterbrechen, die auf jeder anderen Plattform verwendet wird — "
"es muss nach den deklarativen Regeln von ArkTS spielen. Daher ist das "
"harmonyos-Target anders strukturiert:"

#: src/platforms/harmonyos.md:26
msgid ""
"The user splices three artifacts into a DevEco Studio project — "
"`libentry.so`, `pages/Index.ets`, `cpp/types/libentry/Index.d.ts` — and "
"DevEco signs + runs as usual. Tap interactions, text input, etc. fire NAPI "
"calls into the `.so`, which dispatch the registered Perry closure bodies."
msgstr ""
"Der Nutzer spleißt drei Artefakte in ein DevEco Studio-Projekt — "
"`libentry.so`, `pages/Index.ets`, `cpp/types/libentry/Index.d.ts` — und "
"DevEco signiert + führt wie üblich aus. Tap-Interaktionen, Texteingabe usw. "
"lösen NAPI-Aufrufe in die `.so` aus, die die registrierten Perry-Closure-"
"Bodies dispatchen."

