#: src/platforms/wasm.md:75
msgid "FFI Support"
msgstr "FFI-Unterstützung"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:77
msgid ""
"The WASM target supports external FFI functions declared with `declare "
"function`. They become WASM imports under the `\"ffi\"` namespace:"
msgstr ""
"Das WASM-Target unterstützt externe FFI-Funktionen, die mit `declare "
"function` deklariert sind. Sie werden zu WASM-Importen unter dem `\"ffi\"`-"
"Namespace:"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:85
msgid "Provide them when instantiating:"
msgstr "Stellen Sie sie bei der Instanziierung bereit:"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:88
msgid "// Via __ffiImports global (set before boot)"
msgstr "// Über __ffiImports global (vor dem Booten einstellen)"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:90
msgid "// Or via bootPerryWasm second argument"
msgstr "// Oder über bootPerryWasm zweites Argument"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:95
msgid ""
"**Auto-stub for missing imports.** The `ffi` namespace is wrapped in a "
"`Proxy` so any FFI function the host doesn't provide is auto-stubbed with a "
"no-op that returns `TAG_UNDEFINED`. This means apps that use native "
"libraries (e.g. Hone Editor's 56 `hone_editor_*` functions) can still "
"instantiate and run in the browser even without the native bindings — the "
"relevant features are simply no-ops."
msgstr ""
"**Auto-Stub für fehlende Importe.** Der `ffi`-Namespace ist in einen `Proxy` "
"eingewickelt, sodass jede vom Host nicht bereitgestellte FFI-Funktion "
"automatisch mit einem No-op gestubbt wird, das `TAG_UNDEFINED` zurückgibt. "
"Das bedeutet, dass Apps, die native Bibliotheken verwenden (z. B. Hone "
"Editors 56 `hone_editor_*`-Funktionen), auch ohne die nativen Bindungen im "
"Browser instanziieren und laufen können — die betreffenden Features sind "
"einfach No-ops."

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:97
msgid "Module-Level Constants"
msgstr "Modul-Level-Konstanten"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:99
msgid ""
"Top-level `const`/`let` declarations are promoted to dedicated WASM globals "
"so functions in the same module can read them, and so two modules' identical "
"`LocalId`s don't collide:"
msgstr ""
"Top-Level-`const`/`let`-Deklarationen werden zu dedizierten WASM-Globalen "
"befördert, damit Funktionen im selben Modul sie lesen können und damit "
"identische `LocalId`s zweier Module nicht kollidieren:"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:101
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"// telemetry.ts\n"
"const CHIRP_URL = 'https://api.chirp247.com/api/v1/event'\n"
"const API_KEY   = 'my-key'\n"
"\n"
"export function trackEvent(event: string): void {\n"
"    fetch(CHIRP_URL, {\n"
"        method: 'POST',\n"
"        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'X-Chirp-Key': "
"API_KEY },\n"
"        body: JSON.stringify({ event }),\n"
"    })\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"// telemetry.ts\n"
"const CHIRP_URL = 'https://api.chirp247.com/api/v1/event'\n"
"const API_KEY   = 'my-key'\n"
"\n"
"export function trackEvent(event: string): void {\n"
"    fetch(CHIRP_URL, {\n"
"        method: 'POST',\n"
"        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'X-Chirp-Key': "
"API_KEY },\n"
"        body: JSON.stringify({ event }),\n"
"    })\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:115
msgid ""
"Both `CHIRP_URL` and `API_KEY` become WASM globals indexed by `(module_idx, "
"LocalId)`. Reading them from `trackEvent` emits a `global.get` instead of "
"trying to look up a function-local that doesn't exist."
msgstr ""
"Sowohl `CHIRP_URL` als auch `API_KEY` werden zu WASM-Globalen, indiziert "
"nach `(module_idx, LocalId)`. Sie aus `trackEvent` zu lesen emittiert ein "
"`global.get`, statt zu versuchen, ein Funktions-lokales zu suchen, das nicht "
"existiert."

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:117
msgid "JavaScript Runtime Bridge"
msgstr "JavaScript-Runtime-Brücke"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:119
msgid ""
"The bridge (`wasm_runtime.js`) is embedded in the HTML and provides ~280 "
"imports across:"
msgstr ""
"Die Brücke (`wasm_runtime.js`) ist in das HTML eingebettet und stellt ~280 "
"Importe bereit, verteilt auf:"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:121
msgid ""
"**NaN-boxing helpers**: `f64ToU64` / `u64ToF64` / `nanboxString` / "
"`nanboxPointer` / `toJsValue` / `fromJsValue`"
msgstr ""
"**NaN-Boxing-Helfer**: `f64ToU64` / `u64ToF64` / `nanboxString` / "
"`nanboxPointer` / `toJsValue` / `fromJsValue`"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:122
msgid "**String table**: dynamic JS string array indexed by string ID"
msgstr ""
"**String-Tabelle**: dynamisches JS-String-Array, indiziert nach String-ID"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:123
msgid ""
"**Handle store**: maps integer handle IDs to JS objects, arrays, closures, "
"promises, DOM elements"
msgstr ""
"**Handle-Store**: bildet Integer-Handle-IDs auf JS-Objekte, Arrays, "
"Closures, Promises, DOM-Elemente ab"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:124
msgid ""
"**Core ops**: console, math, JSON, JSON.parse/stringify, Date, RegExp, URL, "
"Map, Set, Buffer, fetch"
msgstr ""
"**Kern-Ops**: console, math, JSON, JSON.parse/stringify, Date, RegExp, URL, "
"Map, Set, Buffer, fetch"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:125
msgid ""
"**Closure dispatch**: indirect function table + capture array, with "
"`closure_call_0/1/2/3/spread`"
msgstr ""
"**Closure-Dispatch**: indirekte Funktionstabelle + Capture-Array, mit "
"`closure_call_0/1/2/3/spread`"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:126
msgid ""
"**Class dispatch**: `class_new`, `class_call_method`, `class_get_field`, "
"`class_set_field`, parent table for inheritance"
msgstr ""
"**Class-Dispatch**: `class_new`, `class_call_method`, `class_get_field`, "
"`class_set_field`, Parent-Tabelle für Vererbung"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:127
msgid ""
"**DOM widgets**: 168+ `perry_ui_*` functions covering every widget in `perry/"
"ui`"
msgstr ""
"**DOM-Widgets**: 168+ `perry_ui_*`-Funktionen, die jedes Widget in `perry/"
"ui` abdecken"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:128
msgid ""
"**Async functions**: compiled to JS function bodies and merged into the "
"import object as `__async_<name>`"
msgstr ""
"**Async-Funktionen**: zu JS-Funktionsbodies kompiliert und in das Import-"
"Objekt als `__async_<name>` eingefügt"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:130
msgid ""
"All host imports are wrapped via `wrapImportsForI64()` so they automatically "
"reinterpret BigInt args (from WASM i64 params) into f64 internally and "
"reinterpret Number returns back into BigInt. Without this wrapping, every "
"NaN-valued f64 return would crash with \"Cannot convert NaN to a BigInt\"."
msgstr ""
"Alle Host-Importe werden via `wrapImportsForI64()` umhüllt, sodass sie "
"BigInt-Argumente (aus WASM-i64-Params) automatisch intern in f64 "
"reinterpretieren und Number-Returns zurück in BigInt reinterpretieren. Ohne "
"diese Umhüllung würde jeder NaN-wertige f64-Return mit \"Cannot convert NaN "
"to a BigInt\" crashen."

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:132
msgid "Web Worker Threading"
msgstr "Web-Worker-Threading"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:134
msgid "`perry/thread` works in the browser via a Web Worker pool:"
msgstr "`perry/thread` funktioniert im Browser über einen Web-Worker-Pool:"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:144
msgid ""
"Each worker instantiates its own WASM module with the same bytecode and "
"bridge. Values cross between the main thread and workers via structured-"
"clone serialization. See [Threading](../threading/overview.md)."
msgstr ""
"Jeder Worker instanziiert sein eigenes WASM-Modul mit demselben Bytecode und "
"derselben Brücke. Werte überqueren zwischen dem Main-Thread und den Workern "
"via Structured-Clone-Serialisierung. Siehe [Threading](../threading/"
"overview.md)."

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:148
msgid ""
"**No file system access** beyond the File System Access API "
"(`window.showDirectoryPicker()`)"
msgstr ""
"**Kein Dateisystem-Zugriff** außer über die File System Access API "
"(`window.showDirectoryPicker()`)"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:149
msgid "**No raw TCP/UDP sockets** — only `fetch()` and `WebSocket`"
msgstr "**Keine rohen TCP/UDP-Sockets** — nur `fetch()` und `WebSocket`"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:150
msgid "**No subprocess spawning** — `child_process.exec` etc. are no-ops"
msgstr "**Kein Subprozess-Spawnen** — `child_process.exec` usw. sind No-ops"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:151
msgid ""
"**No native databases** — SQLite, Postgres, MySQL drivers don't compile to "
"web"
msgstr ""
"**Keine nativen Datenbanken** — SQLite-, Postgres-, MySQL-Treiber "
"kompilieren nicht zum Web"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:152
msgid ""
"**CORS** applies to all `fetch()` calls — third-party APIs must allow your "
"origin"
msgstr ""
"**CORS** gilt für alle `fetch()`-Aufrufe — Drittanbieter-APIs müssen Ihren "
"Origin erlauben"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:153
msgid ""
"**localStorage**, not real keychain — fine for preferences, not for secrets"
msgstr ""
"**localStorage**, nicht echter Keychain — ok für Einstellungen, nicht für "
"Geheimnisse"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:154
msgid ""
"Source-mapped stack traces are JS-only; WASM stack frames show `wasm-"
"function[N]`"
msgstr ""
"Source-mapped Stack-Traces sind nur JS; WASM-Stack-Frames zeigen `wasm-"
"function[N]`"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:156
msgid "Minification"
msgstr "Minifizierung"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:158
msgid ""
"Use `--minify` to minify the embedded JS runtime bridge in the HTML output. "
"The Rust-native JS minifier strips comments, collapses whitespace, and "
"mangles internal identifiers, compressing the runtime from ~3,400 lines to "
"~180."
msgstr ""
"Verwenden Sie `--minify`, um die eingebettete JS-Runtime-Brücke in der HTML-"
"Ausgabe zu minifizieren. Der Rust-native JS-Minifier entfernt Kommentare, "
"kollabiert Whitespace und mangelt interne Identifier und komprimiert die "
"Runtime von ~3.400 Zeilen auf ~180."

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:164
msgid "Example: Counter App"
msgstr "Beispiel: Zähler-App"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:187
msgid "Example: Real-World App (Mango MongoDB GUI)"
msgstr "Beispiel: Reale App (Mango MongoDB-GUI)"

#: src/platforms/wasm.md:189
msgid ""
"The [Mango](https://github.com/MangoQuery/app) MongoDB GUI — 50 modules, 998 "
"functions, classes, async functions, fetch with custom headers, the Hone "
"code editor — compiles to a single 4 MB HTML file via `--target web` and "
"renders its full UI (welcome screen, query view, edit view) in the browser. "
"SQLite-backed connection storage gracefully degrades to an in-memory "
"transient store on web; the rest of the app works the same as the native "
"version."
msgstr ""
"Die [Mango](https://github.com/MangoQuery/app) MongoDB GUI — 50 Module, 998 "
"Funktionen, Klassen, async Funktionen, holen mit benutzerdefinierten "
"Headern, den Hone Code Editor — kompiliert zu einer einzigen 4 MB HTML-Datei "
"über `--target web` und rendert seine volle Benutzeroberfläche "
"(Willkommensbildschirm, Abfrageansicht, Bearbeitungsansicht) im Browser. "
"SQLite-Backed-Verbindungsspeicher degradiert anmutig zu einem in-Memory-"
"Transienten-Store im Web; der Rest der App funktioniert genauso wie die "
"native Version."

