msgstr "`no_new_privileges`"

#: src/container/containers.md:62 src/container/security.md:23
msgid ""
"Sets `--security-opt no-new-privileges` — SUID/SGID binaries inside the "
"container can't gain privileges via execve."
msgstr ""
"Sets `--security-opt no-new-privileges` — SUID/SGID Binärdateien innerhalb "
"des Containers können über execve keine Rechte erhalten."

#: src/container/containers.md:64
msgid ""
"When `seccomp` or `no_new_privileges` is set, `run()`/`create()` "
"automatically route through the engine's security-aware launch path (the "
"same one `perry/compose` uses), which also normalizes the spec against the "
"detected backend's capabilities — on apple/container the two flags have no "
"equivalent and are dropped with a warning instead of crashing the CLI. See "
"[Security](./security.md) for the security knobs in depth."
msgstr ""
"Wenn `seccomp` oder `no_new_privileges` gesetzt ist, führt `run()`/"
"`create()` automatisch durch den Sicherheitsstartpfad des Motors (der "
"gleiche `perry/compose` verwendet), der auch die Spezifikation gegen die "
"Fähigkeiten des erkannten Backends normalisiert – auf apple/container haben "
"die beiden Flags kein Äquivalent und werden mit einer Warnung abgesetzt, "
"anstatt das CLI abzustürzen. Siehe [Security](./security.md) für die "
"Sicherheitsknöpfe in der Tiefe."

#: src/container/containers.md:72
msgid "Hardened single-container run"
msgstr "Gehärtete Einzelcontainer-Ausführung"

#: src/container/containers.md:74
msgid ""
"For an untrusted workload (e.g. running user-supplied code, executing a "
"build script from an untrusted source) the recommended starting point is "
"\"drop everything, add back what you need\":"
msgstr ""
"Für einen nicht vertrauenswürdigen Workload (z. B. Ausführung von vom "
"Benutzer bereitgestelltem Code oder eines Build-Skripts aus einer nicht "
"vertrauenswürdigen Quelle) lautet der empfohlene Ausgangspunkt: \"Alles "
"entfernen und nur das Benötigte wieder hinzufügen\":"

#: src/container/containers.md:78 src/container/security.md:46
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"import { run as runSecure } from \"perry/container\";\n"
"\n"
"// Maximum-isolation single-container run for an untrusted workload:\n"
"//   - read-only root filesystem\n"
"//   - no Linux capabilities at all\n"
"//   - non-root user\n"
"//   - working directory pinned\n"
"//   - default seccomp profile\n"
"async function runUntrustedWorkload(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    await runSecure({\n"
"        image: \"alpine:3.19\",\n"
"        cmd: [\"sh\", \"-c\", \"echo isolated && exit 0\"],\n"
"        read_only: true,\n"
"        cap_drop: [\"ALL\"],\n"
"        user: \"nobody\",\n"
"        workdir: \"/tmp\",\n"
"        seccomp: \"default\",\n"
"    });\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"import { run as runSecure } from \"perry/container\";\n"
"\n"
"// Maximum-isolation single-container run for an untrusted workload:\n"
"//   - read-only root filesystem\n"
"//   - no Linux capabilities at all\n"
"//   - non-root user\n"
"//   - working directory pinned\n"
"//   - default seccomp profile\n"
"async function runUntrustedWorkload(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    await runSecure({\n"
"        image: \"alpine:3.19\",\n"
"        cmd: [\"sh\", \"-c\", \"echo isolated && exit 0\"],\n"
"        read_only: true,\n"
"        cap_drop: [\"ALL\"],\n"
"        user: \"nobody\",\n"
"        workdir: \"/tmp\",\n"
"        seccomp: \"default\",\n"
"    });\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/container/containers.md:100
msgid "Inspect, list, logs, exec"
msgstr "Inspizieren, Auflisten, Logs, Exec"

#: src/container/containers.md:102
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"import {\n"
"    list,\n"
"    inspect,\n"
"    logs,\n"
"    exec,\n"
"} from \"perry/container\";\n"
"\n"
"async function inspectAll(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    const containers = await list(true); // all=true → include stopped\n"
"    console.log(containers);\n"
"\n"
"    const id = \"my-container-id\";\n"
"    const info = await inspect(id);\n"
"    console.log(info.status); // \"running\" | \"exited\" | …\n"
"\n"
"    // Tail the last 50 stdout/stderr lines.\n"
"    const tailed = await logs(id, { tail: 50 });\n"
"    console.log(tailed.stdout);\n"
"\n"
"    // Run a command inside the container; returns a ContainerLogs\n"
"    // handle whose stdout/stderr you can read.\n"
"    const r = await exec(id, [\"ls\", \"-la\"]);\n"
"    console.log(r.stdout);\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript\n"
"import {\n"
"    list,\n"
"    inspect,\n"
"    logs,\n"
"    exec,\n"
"} from \"perry/container\";\n"
"\n"
"async function inspectAll(): Promise<void> {\n"
"    const containers = await list(true); // all=true → include stopped\n"
"    console.log(containers);\n"
"\n"
"    const id = \"my-container-id\";\n"
"    const info = await inspect(id);\n"
"    console.log(info.status); // \"running\" | \"exited\" | …\n"
"\n"
"    // Tail the last 50 stdout/stderr lines.\n"
"    const tailed = await logs(id, { tail: 50 });\n"
"    console.log(tailed.stdout);\n"
"\n"
"    // Run a command inside the container; returns a ContainerLogs\n"
"    // handle whose stdout/stderr you can read.\n"
"    const r = await exec(id, [\"ls\", \"-la\"]);\n"
"    console.log(r.stdout);\n"
"}\n"
"```"

