#: src/system/media.md:97
msgid ""
"Stub platforms link cleanly against the same FFI surface — code that imports "
"`perry/media` compiles on every target. `createPlayer` returns `0` on a stub "
"backend so `if (player === 0)` is the canonical \"feature not available "
"here\" check."
msgstr ""
"Stub-Plattformen linken sauber gegen dieselbe FFI-Oberfläche — Code, der "
"`perry/media` importiert, kompiliert auf jedem Target. `createPlayer` gibt "
"auf einem Stub-Backend `0` zurück, sodass `if (player === 0)` die kanonische "
"\"Feature hier nicht verfügbar\"-Prüfung ist."

#: src/system/media.md:102
msgid ""
"On Linux, `setNowPlaying` exposes the player to the desktop via MPRIS "
"(`org.mpris.MediaPlayer2.perry-<pid>` on the session bus). GNOME Shell, KDE "
"Plasma, `playerctl`, and any Bluetooth-headphone media-key bridge that "
"speaks MPRIS will see the metadata and route Play / Pause / PlayPause / "
"Stop / Seek / SetPosition back to the player. The MPRIS server is lazy-"
"bootstrapped on the first `setNowPlaying` call so apps that don't need lock-"
"screen integration don't pay the zbus startup cost. `Next` / `Previous` are "
"no-ops (single-track playback model); playlists are an app-level concern."
msgstr ""
"Auf Linux exponiert `setNowPlaying` den Player gegenüber dem Desktop via "
"MPRIS (`org.mpris.MediaPlayer2.perry-<pid>` auf dem Session-Bus). GNOME "
"Shell, KDE Plasma, `playerctl` und jede Bluetooth-Kopfhörer-Medientasten-"
"Brücke, die MPRIS spricht, sehen die Metadaten und routen Play / Pause / "
"PlayPause / Stop / Seek / SetPosition zurück zum Player. Der MPRIS-Server "
"wird beim ersten `setNowPlaying`-Aufruf lazy gebootstrappt, sodass Apps, die "
"keine Sperrbildschirm-Integration brauchen, nicht die zbus-Startkosten "
"zahlen. `Next` / `Previous` sind No-ops (Single-Track-Wiedergabe-Modell); "
"Playlists sind eine App-Level-Angelegenheit."

#: src/system/media.md:112
msgid "Android — background playback"
msgstr "Android — Hintergrund-Wiedergabe"

#: src/system/media.md:114
msgid ""
"Perry's Android backend wires `MediaSessionCompat` so the lock-screen tile, "
"Bluetooth headset, Android Auto, and Wear OS see the metadata pushed by "
"`setNowPlaying` and route headphone play/pause/stop/seek events back into "
"the registered `onStateChange` closure. That covers foreground use. Apps "
"that want playback to survive the activity being backgrounded (a podcast "
"app, music player, etc.) need a foreground service of their own — Android "
"will otherwise kill the audio when the process drops to the cached state. "
"Add the following to your app's `AndroidManifest.xml` and start the service "
"when playback begins:"
msgstr ""
"Perrys Android-Backend verdrahtet `MediaSessionCompat`, sodass die "
"Sperrbildschirm-Kachel, Bluetooth-Headset, Android Auto und Wear OS die von "
"`setNowPlaying` gepushten Metadaten sehen und Kopfhörer-play/pause/stop/seek-"
"Events zurück in die registrierte `onStateChange`-Closure routen. Das deckt "
"die Vordergrund-Nutzung ab. Apps, die wollen, dass die Wiedergabe das "
"Backgrounden der Activity überlebt (Podcast-App, Musik-Player usw.), "
"brauchen einen eigenen Foreground-Service — Android würde sonst das Audio "
"beenden, wenn der Prozess in den Cached-Zustand fällt. Fügen Sie Folgendes "
"zur `AndroidManifest.xml` Ihrer App hinzu und starten Sie den Service, wenn "
"die Wiedergabe beginnt:"

