#: src/internals/explicit-memory.md:3
msgid ""
"JavaScript has no `free()`. For most programs that's the right default — "
"Perry's generational GC (see [Memory Model](memory-model.md)) decides when "
"to collect. But latency-sensitive programs (games, interactive UIs) and "
"programs that churn large binary buffers sometimes need to _choose the "
"moment_: run the collection between frames, not in the middle of one; "
"release a 100 MB texture now, not at the next full cycle. Perry gives you "
"two standard-shaped tools for that."
msgstr ""
"JavaScript hat keine `free()`. Für die meisten Programme, die die richtige "
"Voreinstellung ist — entscheidet Perry Generation GC (siehe [Speichermodell]"
"(memory-model.md)), wann zu sammeln. Aber Latenz-sensitive Programme "
"(Spiele, interaktive UIs) und Programme, die große binäre Puffer pulnen, "
"müssen manchmal _wählen den Moment_: laufen Sie die Sammlung zwischen "
"Frames, nicht in der Mitte von einem; veröffentlichen Sie jetzt eine 100 MB "
"Textur, nicht im nächsten vollen Zyklus. Perry gibt Ihnen dafür zwei "
"Standard-Werkzeuge."

#: src/internals/explicit-memory.md:10
msgid "`ArrayBuffer.prototype.transfer()` (ES2024)"
msgstr "`ArrayBuffer.prototype.transfer()` (ES2024)"

#: src/internals/explicit-memory.md:12
msgid ""
"`transfer(newLength?)` moves an ArrayBuffer's contents into a new buffer and "
"**detaches** the source: its `byteLength` becomes 0, `detached` reports "
"`true`, views over it report length 0, and any further `transfer`/`slice`/"
"view construction on it throws a `TypeError`. This is standard ECMAScript — "
"the same code runs under Node and Bun unchanged."
msgstr ""
"`transfer(newLength?)` verschiebt den Inhalt eines ArrayBuffer in einen "
"neuen Puffer und **Abhebungen** Die Quelle: seine `byteLength` wird 0, "
"`detached` berichtet `true`, Ansichten über sie berichten Länge 0, und jede "
"weitere `transfer`/`slice` / Ansicht Konstruktion auf es wirft eine "
"`TypeError`. Dies ist der Standard ECMAScript — derselbe Code läuft unter "
"Knoten und Bun unverändert."

#: src/internals/explicit-memory.md:18
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"let scratch = new ArrayBuffer(64 * 1024 * 1024);\n"
"// ... use it ...\n"
"scratch = scratch.transfer(0); // detach: the 64 MB backing is released\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"let scratch = new ArrayBuffer(64 * 1024 * 1024);\n"
"// ... use it ...\n"
"scratch = scratch.transfer(0); // detach: the 64 MB backing is released\n"
"```"

#: src/internals/explicit-memory.md:24
msgid ""
"Perry gives detach real teeth: buffer bytes live inline in the GC heap, so "
"the runtime hands the page-aligned interior of a detached payload back to "
"the OS immediately (`madvise`). A large detached buffer stops costing RSS "
"the moment you transfer it, even while the (now empty) ArrayBuffer object is "
"still reachable. `transferToFixedLength()` behaves identically (Perry has no "
"resizable ArrayBuffers), and `structuredClone(v, { transfer: [...] })` "
"detaches through the same path."
msgstr ""
"Perry gibt echte Zähne ab: Pufferbytes leben inline im GC-Heap, so dass die "
"Laufzeit übergibt die Seite ausgerichteten Innenraum einer losgelösten "
"Nutzlast zurück zum OS sofort (`madvise`). Ein großer freistehender Puffer "
"kostet RSS nicht mehr, wenn Sie ihn übertragen, auch wenn das (jetzt leere) "
"ArrayBuffer-Objekt noch erreichbar ist. `transferToFixedLength()` verhält "
"sich identisch (Perry hat keine resizierbare ArrayBuffers) und "
"`structuredClone(v, { transfer: [...] })` löst sich über denselben Pfad ab."

#: src/internals/explicit-memory.md:32
msgid "`perry/gc` — collection pacing"
msgstr "`perry/gc` — Sammlungsschritte"

#: src/internals/explicit-memory.md:34
msgid ""
"A Perry-native module in the spirit of `perry/thread`: it compiles to direct "
"runtime calls and does not resolve under Node/Bun, so guard the import if "
"the source must also run there."
msgstr ""
"Ein Perry-native-Modul im Geiste von `perry/thread`: Es kompiliert zu "
"direkten Laufzeitaufrufen und löst unter Node/Bun nicht auf, also bewacht "
"den Import, wenn die Quelle auch dort laufen muss."

#: src/internals/explicit-memory.md:38
msgid ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"import { collect, minor, idleHint } from \"perry/gc\";\n"
"\n"
"collect();  // full collection now — same as the global gc()\n"
"minor();    // nursery-only collection now; returns freed bytes\n"
"idleHint(); // \"this is a good moment\": runs a collection only if one\n"
"            // is already due by the normal thresholds; returns whether\n"
"            // one ran. O(1) when nothing is due.\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```typescript,no-test\n"
"import { collect, minor, idleHint } from \"perry/gc\";\n"
"\n"
"collect();  // full collection now — same as the global gc()\n"
"minor();    // nursery-only collection now; returns freed bytes\n"
"idleHint(); // \"this is a good moment\": runs a collection only if one\n"
"            // is already due by the normal thresholds; returns whether\n"
"            // one ran. O(1) when nothing is due.\n"
"```"

#: src/internals/explicit-memory.md:48
msgid ""
"`idleHint()` is the one to reach for in a frame loop: call it once per frame "
"after presenting. When allocation pressure has made a collection imminent, "
"it runs at your chosen boundary instead of landing mid-frame at whatever "
"allocation happens to trip the threshold:"
msgstr ""
